# LULU Pitch Deck Copy Is Verbatim (Slides 2-13)

Slides 2-13 of `LULU_Investment_Pitch_Deck.pptx` (slide 8 = "Slide 7 Part 2")
are user-authored. The title, descriptor, every bullet, and every
`Links & Sources` entry must appear **word for word**. Do not paraphrase,
summarize, reorder, drop citation markers, or "institutionalize" the wording.

## Single source of truth

`LULU/slide_copy_source.txt` is the user's slide text pasted verbatim.
`LULU/scripts/verify_slide_copy.py` parses that file — it does not restate the
copy — and checks the built deck against it. When the user supplies new slide
text, replace `slide_copy_source.txt` first, then mirror it in
`build_pitch.py`.

## Required after any deck rebuild

```bash
cd LULU/scripts && python3 build_pitch.py && python3 verify_slide_copy.py
```

The verifier must print `PASS`. A `MISSING` line means a word/citation was
dropped or altered — fix `build_pitch.py`, never `slide_copy_source.txt`
(unless the user changed the copy).

## Allowed deviations only

- En/em dashes (`–` `—`) render as hyphens (`-`) and curly quotes render
  straight. These are the only permitted character substitutions; both are
  normalized in the verifier.
- A bullet may drop a trailing sentence period, and slide 13 may split a
  `Label: body` line into a label shape plus a body shape.
- No `→` arrows, no AI em-dashes, no added/removed words otherwise.

## Citation placement

Every citation marker (`[1]`, `[2]`, ...) stays at the **end of its sentence**,
exactly as in the source.
